      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "0.25 mmol of (E)-2-(2-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzylideneamino)phenol (H2L1) was added to 0.125 mmol of (+)-3-trifluoroacetyl camphor (D-Htfc) in 5 mL of DMF and 25 mL of MeCN. After stirring for 10 min, 0.25 mmol of Dy(CF3SO3)3 and 0.75 mmol of Et3N were added successively. The mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature, forming an orange-yellow solution that was filtered into a beaker and crystallized by slow solvent evaporation. After several days, brown single crystals of D-1 were harvested.",
